{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK5GLT4XG8fZzDXuvddi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `addMonths` in `dates.js`. Jan 31 + 1 month now lands on Feb 28 (or Feb 29 in a leap year) instead of rolling over into March.\n\n**The cause:** `setMonth` doesn't clamp. Jan 31 + 1 became Feb 31, which overflowed to Mar 3. Billing dates on the 29th–31st were being pushed into the following month.\n\n**The change:** I move the date to the 1st before calling `setMonth`, then clamp the original day to the target month's last day. Time of day and the input object are preserved, as before.\n\n**Checks I ran with Node:**\n- Jan 31 10:30 + 1 → Feb 28 2026 10:30\n- Jan 15 + 1 → Feb 15 2026 (unchanged)\n- Jan 31 − 1 → Dec 31 2025\n- Jan 31 2024 + 1 → Feb 29 2024 (leap year)\n- Mar 31 − 1 → Feb 28 2026\n\nThis is not a git repo, so I haven't run the project's test suite. I didn't check whether anything else depends on the old overflow behaviour."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1215,"cache_read_input_tokens":23671,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1215},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a7fa7c8-148e-406b-8d57-cc81fbb85e75","uuid":"3da4831d-4348-496b-a6ab-7ca63db1b1ec","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:30:59.027Z","request_id":"req_011ChK5GLGPJE6o5GVY6pAXc"}
